{{end}}
---

## 2.9 Infrastructure

Default local infrastructure:

```txt
Docker Compose
```

The project must run locally with:

```bash
docker compose up
```

or an equivalent documented command.

The local environment should require no manual post-install configuration.

The setup should automatically handle:

- database creation
- migrations
- seed data
- initial admin user when applicable
- MinIO bucket creation
- RabbitMQ exchanges and queues
- Redis service
- observability provisioning when enabled
- Keycloak realm import when Keycloak is used

Future production evolution may use:

- K3s
- Kubernetes
- Longhorn
- Helm
- Tailscale
- VPS gateway
- self-hosted home server

But Kubernetes must not be required for local development.

