# 18. Forbidden Changes Without Explicit Approval

Do not introduce these without explicit approval:

- Nest.js
- Next.js
- chi
- gin
- echo
- fiber
- Ent
- GORM
- Prisma
- NATS
- Kafka
- ELK
- MongoDB
- GraphQL
- microservices split
- Kubernetes-only local development
- hardcoded UI strings
- Portuguese identifiers in code
- browser-stored access tokens
- manual-only infrastructure setup

---

# 19. Definition of Done

A task is complete only when:

- the change follows this `AGENTS.md`
- the code builds
- relevant tests pass
- user-facing strings are localized
- no hardcoded UI text was introduced
- APIs return stable error codes
- OpenAPI was updated when contracts changed
- migrations were added when schema changed
- sqlc was regenerated when queries changed
- docs were updated in both languages when needed
- no forbidden dependency was introduced
- logs and internal messages remain in English
- security boundaries were preserved
- the work is small enough to review

---

# 20. Project Philosophy

Prefer explicit code over magic.

Prefer standard library over unnecessary frameworks.

Prefer SQL over hidden ORM behavior.

Prefer modular monolith over premature microservices.

Prefer Docker Compose first.

Prefer Kubernetes later only when justified.

Prefer self-hostable infrastructure.

Prefer stable contracts.

Prefer auditability.

Prefer boring, reliable technology.

Prefer code that AI agents and humans can both understand.

The default answer to unnecessary complexity is no.
